{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/342992-one-million-shuankhsen","id":342992,"title":"One Million Shuankhsen!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-17T08:54:05-08:00","id":342992,"title":"One Million Shuankhsen!","content":"So I just came across this: <a href=\"http://rt.com/news/215115-egypt-million-mummies-discovered/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rt.com/news/215115-egypt-mill...es-discovered/</a><br /> <br /> Sounds...flabbergasting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:59:47-08:00","id":343006,"title":"","content":"I feel as if every Arisen with an internet connection just wet themselves and ran into their tombs to wait out this Turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:06:22-08:00","id":343011,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they were trying to re-create a Mass Rite of Return, a la a D&amp;D spell, or if they just gathered all the Lifeless they could and dumped them in a hole and hoped they were never disturbed or clawed themselves out during a Turn. Suuuuper good plot hooks from this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T13:08:52-08:00","id":343155,"title":"","content":"You're right there. That first picture, the one of the eighteen month old girl, just had me wondering if there are any infant/child Shuankhsen around. It certainly seems possible. Arisen were selected due to their prowess in their respective Guilds, but the Shuankhsen needed no such qualifications. Wouldn't be hard to justify murderous children with big, big teeth stalking Arisen down through the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:38:20-08:00","id":343445,"title":"","content":"Man, would child souls even survive Duat long enough to make it to Ammut? You would think the Slaughterers would have gotten to them before they were so unfortunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:43:32-08:00","id":343448,"title":"","content":"I dunno, is there any reason to presume the strength of the soul is in any way linked to physical prowess in life? Or age, for that matter? Many of the Arisen are quite young (which is to be expected, given that you were probably considered an adult by 12/14). And the Shuankhsen are described as descending to Ammut in mobs, so if the child managed to get near the centre of the group...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:20:57-08:00","id":343468,"title":"","content":"I'd say no to physical prowess, yes to age, if only because a lot of it seems to do with identity and children are still in the early stages of identity formation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:28:03-08:00","id":343472,"title":"","content":"While possible, I always felt that those souls that reached Ammut did so by luck more than strength. Child Shuankhsen wouldn't be common, but there's always a... &quot;lucky&quot; one.<br /> <br /> I mean, come on. It's a fantastically disturbing idea.<br /> <br /> Mind you, even if the Shuankhsen is an adult, there's nothing stopping their cultists summoning their master into a child/infant's body. Probably not the norm, but it could be useful for a particularly tricky bit of infiltration.<br /> <br /> And conversely, a child's soul (perhaps locked in development a bit over the last 6,000 years) inside an adult's body is fairly creepy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T18:42:30-08:00","id":343530,"title":"","content":"Anything is possible, I suppose, but I have a hard time imagining any of the Deathless as children unless their original bodies were destroyed and they were resurrected into a child's corpse. It would certainly make for an interesting flashback if, as a PC Mummy, your GM was like, &quot;Oh, by the way, this time around? You're eleven years old.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shuankhsen, though? I don't think the Devourer is too picky; I can easily see a few children getting tossed into the sacrificial arena, by intent or by accident. Most children might be kept around to become indoctrinated into the Empire's creed, but certainly not all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}